tps://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/long-before-ants-began-caring-for-their-young-the-same-brain-circuits-were-helping-them-find-food/articleshow/132660770.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-27T17:34:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132660770,imgsize-1731366.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Elon Musk says a future on Mars could help humanity survive pandemics, AI and global disasters]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132658806.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Elon Musk believes a Mars colony can protect humanity from global disasters.  He argues the vast distance offers a crucial buffer against pandemics and cyber threats.  A six-month journey to Mars acts as an automatic quarantine period for diseases.  Digital attacks also face significant delays, providing time for mitigation efforts.  This expansion ensures human civilization is not solely confined to one planet.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/elon-musk-says-a-future-on-mars-could-help-humanity-survive-pandemics-ai-and-global-disasters/articleshow/132658806.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/elon-musk-says-a-future-on-mars-could-help-humanity-survive-pandemics-ai-and-global-disasters/articleshow/132658806.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-27T16:04:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132658933,imgsize-56791.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Joni Mitchell’s former Malibu home is listed for $27 million; its beachfront pool may be impossible to recreate today]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-righ